        <div class="card" style="margin-top:1.5rem">
          <h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.2rem;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:1rem">Which cooking method has the fewest calories?</h2>
          <p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:0.75rem">Boiled, soft-boiled and poached eggs are useful options if you want to prepare eggs without adding cooking fat. Scrambled eggs can also have a similar calorie content when made without oil, butter, milk or other calorie-containing ingredients.</p>
          <p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:0.75rem">Fried eggs tend to contain more calories because of the oil or butter used in the pan. The difference depends on how much fat is added and how much ends up in the finished serving.</p>
          <p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.8">If you are counting calories, remember to include any oil, butter, cheese, milk or other ingredients added to your eggs. The cooking method alone does not tell you the exact nutritional value of the finished dish.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card" style="margin-top:1.5rem">
          <h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.2rem;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:1rem">How to calculate calories in eggs</h2>
          <p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:0.75rem">To estimate the calories in a serving, choose the approximate value for one egg of your size and cooking method, then multiply it by the number of eggs. Add the calories from oil and other ingredients separately if they are not already included in the estimate.</p>
          <p style="font-size:0.95rem;line-height:1.8;margin-bottom:0.75rem"><strong>Total calories = calories per egg × number of eggs + calories from additional ingredients</strong></p>
          <p style="color:var(--muted);font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.8">For example, two medium boiled eggs provide approximately 154 calories using this calculator's estimates. Two medium fried eggs with a little oil provide approximately 224 calories, although the actual total will depend on the amount of oil used.</p>
