      <aside class="calc-sidebar">
        <div class="card sidebar-card">
          <h2>Egg white vs yolk: what's the difference?</h2>
          <p>The egg white contains protein and very little fat, making it lower in calories than the yolk. The yolk provides more calories and contains most of the egg's fat, as well as nutrients such as vitamin D and vitamin B12. Eating the whole egg provides nutrients from both parts.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="card sidebar-card">
          <h3>Frequently asked questions</h3>

          <details>
            <summary>How many calories are in a boiled egg?</summary>
            <p>A medium boiled egg contains approximately 77 calories using this calculator's estimates. A small egg has around 62 calories, while a large egg has around 91 calories. The exact amount depends on the egg's edible weight.</p>
          </details>

          <details>
            <summary>How many calories are in a fried egg?</summary>
            <p>A medium fried egg may contain around 112 calories when prepared with a little oil, or about 137 calories with a larger amount. These are estimates, since the calories depend on how much cooking fat is used and retained.</p>
          </details>

          <details>
            <summary>How many calories are in 2 eggs?</summary>
            <p>Two medium boiled eggs contain approximately 154 calories. Two large boiled eggs contain around 182 calories. Fried eggs generally contain more calories because of the added cooking fat.</p>
          </details>

          <details>
            <summary>How many calories are in 3 eggs?</summary>
            <p>Three medium boiled eggs contain approximately 231 calories. Three large boiled eggs provide around 273 calories. Add any oil, butter or other ingredients used during preparation.</p>
          </details>

          <details>
            <summary>How many calories are in an egg white?</summary>
            <p>The white of a medium egg contains approximately 17 calories and 3.6g of protein in the reference values shown above. It contains very little fat compared with the yolk.</p>
          </details>

          <details>
            <summary>How many calories are in an egg yolk?</summary>
            <p>The yolk of a medium egg contains approximately 55 calories in the reference values shown above. It provides much of the egg's fat and contains nutrients including vitamin D and vitamin B12.</p>
          </details>

          <details>
            <summary>Do eggs have more calories when cooked?</summary>
            <p>Boiling or poaching an egg without additional ingredients does not substantially increase its total calories. Frying eggs or scrambling them with oil, butter, milk or other ingredients adds calories from those ingredients.</p>
          </details>

          <details>
            <summary>Are eggs a good source of protein?</summary>
            <p>Yes. A medium egg provides approximately 6.5g of protein in this calculator's reference values. Both the white and the yolk contain protein, although the white provides more protein relative to its calories.</p>
          </details>

          <details>
            <summary>Are eggs suitable for weight management?</summary>
            <p>Eggs provide protein and can be part of a balanced diet. Whether they fit a particular weight goal depends on overall energy intake, portion sizes and the rest of your eating pattern.</p>
          </details>

          <details>
            <summary>Does the egg size include the shell?</summary>
            <p>The size ranges displayed in the calculator refer to the weight of the egg with its shell. The nutritional estimates represent the edible egg, so they are approximate rather than a direct calculation from the full shell-on weight.</p>
          </details>
        </div>

